$sum_(n=1)^oo (1)/(n^2)$ converges:
$
  sum_(n=1)^oo (1)/(n^2) = 1 + sum_(n=2)^oo (1)/(n^2) <= 1 + sum_(n=1)^oo (1)/((n+1)^2) <= 1 + sum_(n=1)^oo (1)/(n(n+1)) < oo,
$
where $sum 1/(n(n+1))$ converges with partial sums $1 - (1)/(k+1) -> 1$. Comparison with this convergent dominating series settles the question.
